    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Romanian parliament raised the country to a kingdom in 1881, three years after the Treaty of Berlin recognised its independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</li><li>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukovina">Bukovina</a> joined the kingdom, and by 1920 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> was more than twice its 1914 size.</li><li>Carol II's royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> of 1938 gave way in 1940 to the military dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-antonescu">Ion Antonescu</a>, and the monarchy was abolished on 30 December 1947.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1857, before the kingdom existed, the first oil refinery in the world was built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ploiesti">Ploiești</a>; by the late 1930s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> was one of the top oil exporters.</p></aside>
    </section>

